// nf-core/ampliseq 3.1.0 on Apple silicon with conda/mamba (osx-arm64). Used by run_study.py only
// when NF_PROFILE is conda or mamba.
//
// All 82 module environments were dry-run solved for osx-arm64 on 2026-11-14 (conda-forge +
// bioconda): 71 solve as pinned. Of the 11 that don't, only these are on our path:
//   * CUTADAPT_SUMMARY_*: pins python=3.8.3, which has no osx-arm64 build. Its script
//     (bin/cutadapt_summary.py) only imports re and sys, so the last 3.8 release is a safe swap.
//   * PHYLOSEQ_INASV (sed=4.7) and TREESUMMARIZEDEXPERIMENT (needs bioconductor-biocparallel 1.36):
//     avoided with skip_phyloseq / skip_tse in params.json; the R objects are not needed because
//     the database tables are the output.
//   * SUMMARY_REPORT solves (R 4.2.3) but fails at run time: rmarkdown cannot load rlang.dylib.
//     Avoided with skip_report; MultiQC and pipeline_qc.json cover QC.
// The other 8 (QIIME2 export, decontam, ITS, length filters, phylogenetic placement) are not run.
process {
    withName: 'CUTADAPT_SUMMARY_STD|CUTADAPT_SUMMARY_DOUBLEPRIMER' {
        conda = 'conda-forge::python=3.8.20'
    }
}
